            <ArticleTitle>The stiff total knee arthroplasty: causes and cures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>103-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1302/0301-620X.94B11.30793</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Seven stiff total knee arthroplasties are presented to illustrate the roles of: 1) manipulation under general anesthesia; 2) multiple concurrent diagnoses in addition to stiffness; 3) extra-articular pathology; 4) pain as part of the stiffness triad (pain and limits to flexion or extension); 5) component internal rotation; 6) multifactorial etiology; and 7) surgical exposure in this challenging clinical problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
